<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lpdf version="1"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../../schema/lpdf.xsd">
  <tokens>
    <colors>
      <color name="primary" value="#1763cf"/>
      <color name="accent"  value="#e8f0fc"/>
      <color name="muted"   value="#737373"/>
      <color name="rule"    value="#dde3ed"/>
    </colors>
  </tokens>
  <document size="a4" margin="56pt">
    <meta title="lpdf Showcase — Bookmarks and Table of Contents"
          subject="bookmark, section type=toc and href=#id links"/>

    <!-- Layer-only cover: the section's own bookmark marks its page -->
    <section margin="0pt">
      <bookmark label="Cover"/>
      <layer>
        <rect x="0pt" y="0pt" w="595pt" h="842pt" fill="primary"/>
        <text x="56pt" y="380pt" font-size="32pt" font="Helvetica-Bold" color="#ffffff">Annual Report</text>
        <text x="56pt" y="420pt" font-size="14pt" color="accent">Bookmarks, internal links and a table of contents</text>
      </layer>
    </section>

    <!-- Table of contents: laid out after the other sections, bound to $toc -->
    <section type="toc" toc-indent-step="16pt">
      <bookmark label="Contents" id="contents"/>
      <layout>
        <column gap="m">
          <text font-size="xl" font="Helvetica-Bold" color="primary">Contents</text>
          <divider color="rule" thickness="xs"/>
          <column gap="xs">
            <column data-source="$toc">
              <link href="#">
                <row justify="between">
                  <text data-value="label">Entry</text>
                  <text data-value="page" color="muted">0</text>
                </row>
              </link>
            </column>
          </column>
        </column>
      </layout>
    </section>

    <section>
      <layout>
        <bookmark label="Introduction"/>
        <text font-size="l" font="Helvetica-Bold" color="primary">Introduction</text>
        <text>
          This document shows the bookmarks of a PDF: each heading has a bookmark before it, which puts it in the
          viewer's bookmark panel and gives links a place to jump to. The contents page lists them with their page
          numbers, which the engine works out after laying out the rest of the document.
        </text>
        <bookmark label="Background" level="2"/>
        <text font-size="m" font="Helvetica-Bold">Background</text>
        <text>
          A bookmark draws nothing. It marks the element that follows it, so a heading pushed to the next page takes
          its bookmark along. See <span href="#methods" color="primary" underline="true">Methods</span> for how
          the numbers are found, or go back to the <span href="#contents" color="primary" underline="true">contents</span>.
        </text>
      </layout>
    </section>

    <section>
      <layout>
        <bookmark label="Methods"/>
        <text font-size="l" font="Helvetica-Bold" color="primary">Methods</text>
        <text>
          The table of contents is laid out last. Its own length moves the pages after it, so it is laid out again
          with that length counted, until the length holds.
        </text>
        <bookmark label="Data Collection" level="2"/>
        <text font-size="m" font="Helvetica-Bold">Data Collection</text>
        <text>Entries below the first level are indented by toc-indent-step for each level.</text>
        <bookmark label="Sampling" level="3"/>
        <text font-size="m" font="Helvetica-Bold">Sampling</text>
        <text>A third level nests under the second, in the outline and in the contents.</text>
      </layout>
    </section>

    <section>
      <layout>
        <bookmark label="Results"/>
        <text font-size="l" font="Helvetica-Bold" color="primary">Results</text>
        <text>Every entry in the contents is a link to its bookmark.</text>
      </layout>
    </section>

  </document>
</lpdf>
